--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Material in this repository by other hands
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

proverif/
    The three ProVerif models are the work of Frederic Lafitte and are
    included here with his permission. They are the models printed in
    Appendices B, C and D of the accompanying paper, carried in this
    repository so that a reader can run what the paper prints. They are
    formal models rather than part of the implementation, and nothing in the
    implementation depends on them.

encryption/ascon.py
    pyascon, the Python reference implementation of Ascon by Maria
    Eichlseder, https://github.com/meichlseder/pyascon, released under the
    Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal public domain dedication. CC0
    imposes no attribution requirement; the credit is given as a matter of
    academic practice. The Ascon specification itself is the work of
    Christoph Dobraunig, Maria Eichlseder, Florian Mendel and Martin
    Schlaeffer, standardised as NIST SP 800-232.

Ed25519 signatures and X25519 key agreement are performed by the `cryptography`
package (pyca/cryptography), which is not included here and is installed as a
dependency under its own licence (Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause, at the user's
option). Transport uses `paho-mqtt`, likewise installed as a dependency, under
the Eclipse Public License 2.0 and the Eclipse Distribution License 1.0.
